 142:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****                  ##### Peripheral Control functions #####
 143:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================
 144:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 145:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****      [..]
 146:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****      *** PVD configuration ***
 147:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     =========================
 148:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 149:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) The PVD is used to monitor the VDD power supply by comparing it to a
 150:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           threshold selected by the PVD Level (PLS[2:0] bits in PWR_CR2 register).
 151:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 152:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) PVDO flag is available to indicate if VDD/VDDA is higher or lower
 153:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           than the PVD threshold. This event is internally connected to the EXTI
 154:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           line16 and can generate an interrupt if enabled. This is done through
 155:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           __HAL_PWR_PVD_EXTI_ENABLE_IT() macro.
 156:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) The PVD is stopped in Standby mode.
 157:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 158:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 159:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     *** WakeUp pin configuration ***
 160:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     ================================
 161:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 162:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) WakeUp pins are used to wakeup the system from Standby mode.
 163:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           The polarity of these pins can be set to configure event detection on high
 164:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           level (rising edge) or low level (falling edge).
 165:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 166:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 167:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 168:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     *** Low Power modes configuration ***
 169:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     =====================================
 170:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 171:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       The devices feature 7 low-power modes:
 172:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Low-power Run mode: core and peripherals are running, main regulator off, low power regul
 173:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Sleep mode: Cortex-M4 core stopped, peripherals kept running, main and low power regulato
 174:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Low-power Sleep mode: Cortex-M4 core stopped, peripherals kept running, main regulator of
 175:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Stop 0 mode: all clocks are stopped except LSI and LSE, main and low power regulators on.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\n11ak\AppData\Local\Temp\ccatqfKb.s 			page 6


 176:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Stop 1 mode: all clocks are stopped except LSI and LSE, main regulator off, low power reg
 177:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Standby mode with SRAM2: all clocks are stopped except LSI and LSE, SRAM2 content preserv
 178:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Standby mode without SRAM2: all clocks are stopped except LSI and LSE, main and low power
 179:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 180:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Low-power run mode ***
 181:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    ==========================
 182:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 183:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry: (from main run mode)
 184:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         (++) set LPR bit with HAL_PWREx_EnableLowPowerRunMode() API after having decreased the syst
 185:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 186:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 187:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         (++) clear LPR bit then wait for MR_RDY bit to be set with HAL_PWREx_DisableLowPowerRunMode
 188:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****              then can the system clock frequency be increased above 2 MHz.
 189:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 190:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 191:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Sleep mode / Low-power sleep mode ***
 192:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    =========================================
 193:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 194:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 195:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           The Sleep mode / Low-power Sleep mode is entered through HAL_PWR_EnterSLEEPMode() API
 196:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           in specifying whether or not the regulator is forced to low-power mode and if exit is int
 197:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_MAINREGULATOR_ON: Sleep mode (regulator in main mode).
 198:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_LOWPOWERREGULATOR_ON: Low-power sleep (regulator in low power mode).
 199:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           In the latter case, the system clock frequency must have been decreased below 2 MHz befor
 200:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFI: enter SLEEP mode with WFI instruction
 201:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFE: enter SLEEP mode with WFE instruction
 202:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 203:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) WFI Exit:
 204:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         (++) Any peripheral interrupt acknowledged by the nested vectored interrupt
 205:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****              controller (NVIC) or any wake-up event.
 206:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 207:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) WFE Exit:
 208:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         (++) Any wake-up event such as an EXTI line configured in event mode.
 209:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 210:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****          [..] When exiting the Low-power sleep mode by issuing an interrupt or a wakeup event,
 211:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****              the MCU is in Low-power Run mode.
 212:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 213:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Stop 0, Stop 1 modes ***
 214:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    ===============================
 215:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 216:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 217:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           The Stop 0, Stop 1 modes are entered through the following API's:
 218:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) HAL_PWREx_EnterSTOP0Mode() for mode 0 or HAL_PWREx_EnterSTOP1Mode() for mode 1 or fo
 219:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Regulator setting (applicable to HAL_PWR_EnterSTOPMode() only):
 220:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_MAINREGULATOR_ON
 221:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_LOWPOWERREGULATOR_ON
 222:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit (interrupt or event-triggered, specified when entering STOP mode):
 223:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFI: enter Stop mode with WFI instruction
 224:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFE: enter Stop mode with WFE instruction
 225:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 226:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) WFI Exit:
 227:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) Any EXTI Line (Internal or External) configured in Interrupt mode.
 228:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) Some specific communication peripherals (LPUART, I2C) interrupts
 229:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****                when programmed in wakeup mode.
 230:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) WFE Exit:
 231:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) Any EXTI Line (Internal or External) configured in Event mode.
 232:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
ARM GAS  C:\Users\n11ak\AppData\Local\Temp\ccatqfKb.s 			page 7


 233:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****        [..]
 234:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           When exiting Stop 0 and Stop 1 modes, the MCU is either in Run mode or in Low-power Run m
 235:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           depending on the LPR bit setting.
 236:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 237:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Standby mode ***
 238:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    ====================
 239:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****      [..]
 240:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       The Standby mode offers two options:
 241:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) option a) all clocks off except LSI and LSE, RRS bit set (keeps voltage regulator in low 
 242:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         SRAM and registers contents are lost except for the SRAM2 content, the RTC registers, RTC b
 243:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         and Standby circuitry.
 244:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) option b) all clocks off except LSI and LSE, RRS bit cleared (voltage regulator then disa
 245:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         SRAM and register contents are lost except for the RTC registers, RTC backup registers
 246:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         and Standby circuitry.
 247:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 248:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) Entry:
 249:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (+++) The Standby mode is entered through HAL_PWR_EnterSTANDBYMode() API.
 250:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****                 SRAM1 and register contents are lost except for registers in the Backup domain and
 251:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****                 Standby circuitry. SRAM2 content can be preserved if the bit RRS is set in PWR_CR3 
 252:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****                 To enable this feature, the user can resort to HAL_PWREx_EnableSRAM2ContentRetentio
 253:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****                 to set RRS bit.
 254:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 255:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) Exit:
 256:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****           (+++) WKUP pin rising edge, RTC alarm or wakeup, tamper event,
 257:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****                 external reset in NRST pin, IWDG reset.
 258:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 259:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       [..]    After waking up from Standby mode, program execution restarts in the same way as afte
 260:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 261:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 262:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Auto-wakeup (AWU) from low-power mode ***
 263:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****    =============================================
 264:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 265:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       The MCU can be woken up from low-power mode by an RTC Alarm event, an RTC
 266:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       Wakeup event, a tamper event, without depending on
 267:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       an external interrupt (Auto-wakeup mode).
 268:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 269:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) RTC auto-wakeup (AWU) from the Stop and Standby modes
 270:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 271:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 272:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with an RTC alarm event, it is necessary to
 273:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****              configure the RTC to generate the RTC alarm using the HAL_RTC_SetAlarm_IT() function.
 274:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 275:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****         (++) To wake up from the Stop mode with an RTC Tamper, it
 276:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****              is necessary to configure the RTC to detect the tamper using the
 277:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****              HAL_RTCEx_SetTamper_IT() functions.
 278:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 279:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
