 399:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 400:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** 
 401:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c **** /**
 402:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   * @brief Enter Sleep or Low-power Sleep mode.
 403:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note  In Sleep/Low-power Sleep mode, all I/O pins keep the same state as in Run mode.
 404:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   * @param Regulator: Specifies the regulator state in Sleep/Low-power Sleep mode.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\n11ak\AppData\Local\Temp\ccatqfKb.s 			page 14


 405:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *          This parameter can be one of the following values:
 406:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *            @arg @ref PWR_MAINREGULATOR_ON Sleep mode (regulator in main mode)
 407:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *            @arg @ref PWR_LOWPOWERREGULATOR_ON Low-power Sleep mode (regulator in low-power mode
 408:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note  Low-power Sleep mode is entered from Low-power Run mode. Therefore, if not yet
 409:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *        in Low-power Run mode before calling HAL_PWR_EnterSLEEPMode() with Regulator set
 410:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *        to PWR_LOWPOWERREGULATOR_ON.
 411:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *        Additionally, the clock frequency must be reduced below 2 MHz.
 412:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note  When exiting Low-power Sleep mode, the MCU is in Low-power Run mode. To move in
 413:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *        Run mode, the user must resort to HAL_PWREx_DisableLowPowerRunMode() API.
 414:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   * @param SLEEPEntry: Specifies if Sleep mode is entered with WFI or WFE instruction.
 415:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *           This parameter can be one of the following values:
 416:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *            @arg @ref PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFI enter Sleep or Low-power Sleep mode with WFI instructio
 417:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   *            @arg @ref PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFE enter Sleep or Low-power Sleep mode with WFE instructio
 418:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note  When WFI entry is used, tick interrupt have to be disabled if not desired as
